        "path": "/Plantae/Tracheophytes/Angiosperms/Monocots/Asparagales/Asphodelaceae/Asphodeloideae/Kniphofia",
        "scenario": "general.botanicExample",
        "link": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kniphofia",
        "description": "Kniphofia (/n\u026ap\u02c8ho\u028afi\u0259/, /n\u026a\u02c8fo\u028afi\u0259/) is a genus of perennial flowering plants in the family Asphodelaceae, first described as a genus in 1794. All species of Kniphofia are native to Africa. Common names include tritoma, red hot poker, torch lily and poker plant."
